<title>UK: Banco Santiago's Yankee bond expected soon.</title>
<headline>Banco Santiago's Yankee bond expected soon.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco Santiago, the largest bank in Chile, is expected to launch a subordinated Yankee bond next week, bankers said on Friday.</p>
<p>The offering is expected to be for $200 million with a 10-year maturity.</p>
<p>UBS is the lead manager.</p>
<p>Recently, Moody's Investors Service assigned a rating of Baa1 to Banco Santiago's $200 million subordinated note issue.</p>
<p>Standard &amp; Poor's rated the notes BBB.</p>
<p>-- Hayley Pienaar, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7718</p>
</text>
